  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})-1?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x$ is given by\n\n$$\nx\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})-1,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.",
